{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>The people have sinned, etc.</b> Perhaps it intends to say by way of the statement of those of blessed memory (Sotah 3a) that a person does not commit a transgression unless a spirit of folly enters him, and this is the lack of the soul. And this is His saying <b>have sinned</b> — meaning, they were diminished from the illumination of their soul, and because of this, ״they made for themselves,״ etc. And this is one of the arguments by which a person is vindicated on the day of judgment, for in committing the sin his mind was not whole; and even though he will be punished for having caused the diminution to himself through twisted thoughts, nevertheless it will not be comparable to being judged for the evil deed with his whole mind." "<b>Further,</b> it intends according to what has preceded us (Kiddushin 40a), that for idolatry a person is punished even for the thought alone. And thus He said, corresponding to the thought: <b>this people have sinned</b>, and corresponding to the deed He said <b>and they made for themselves</b>, etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:14.759959908Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}